From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 22:28:27 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: kaanapali-oneplus-iceland: give the
 touchscreen its physical size

The panel's active area is 274 x 193 mm (the DSI connector reports it); with "touchscreen-x-mm" and
"touchscreen-y-mm" the nt36536 driver sets a resolution on the touch and pen axes (33920 x 24000 units), which
libinput requires for the pen and the compositors use for the touch-to-output mapping.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
index 792664acc9dd..5055138d8310 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
@@ -1396,6 +1396,10 @@
 
 		novatek,pen-support;
 
+		/* the panel is 274 x 193 mm: a resolution for the touch and pen axes */
+		touchscreen-x-mm = <274>;
+		touchscreen-y-mm = <193>;
+
 		panel = <&display_panel>;
 
 		firmware-name = "novatek/novatek_nt36536_fw.bin";
